WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.791 --> 00:00:18.394
Jonathan nearly bumped into Marissa on his way to the school cafeteria on Monday.

2
00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:24.098
He flashed her a smile, but Marissa's eyes narrowed before she quickly looked away and rushed past him.

3
00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:28.842
Jonathan knew he had to do something about her.

4
00:00:29.523 --> 00:00:30.344
And about her father.

5
00:00:31.084 --> 00:00:34.005
He needed to grow a backbone—a very large backbone.

6
00:00:35.005 --> 00:00:39.426
He was so distracted at lunchtime, he dipped his French fries in milk instead of ketchup, and he

7
00:00:39.466 --> 00:00:41.567
bit into his orange before remembering to peel it.

8
00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:47.808
Later he got out his history textbook in science class and accidentally went to his English classroom when

9
00:00:47.828 --> 00:00:48.709
it was time for math.

10
00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:51.750
It took him forever to do his homework after school.

11
00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.671
Whenever he looked at his books, all he saw were soccer balls and Marissa's pretty face.

12
00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:00.732
During dinner that night, Jonathan's mother frowned.

13
00:01:01.556 --> 00:01:03.858
"You love meatloaf, but you've hardly touched it tonight.

14
00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:05.640
What's the matter, Johnnyboy?"

15
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.042
"Please don't call me that, Mom.

16
00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:10.664
I'm not a baby anymore," Jonathan said.

17
00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:13.106
"I'll try not to," Mrs.

18
00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:13.807
Cho promised.

19
00:01:13.827 --> 00:01:15.428
"But tell me what's wrong."

20
00:01:16.028 --> 00:01:17.730
Jonathan speared his meatloaf with his fork.

21
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.054
"I wish I were on a different soccer team," he muttered.

22
00:01:23.014 --> 00:01:24.396
Mr. Cho nodded his agreement.

23
00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:26.337
"I wish you were too.

24
00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:29.320
I don't like how your coach is running things," he said.

25
00:01:30.272 --> 00:01:33.275
"I'll call him tomorrow and tell him to give you and the other boys more chances with the

26
00:01:33.315 --> 00:01:37.158
ball." "Good idea," Jonathan's mother said.

27
00:01:37.178 --> 00:01:40.441
"I'll talk to him too and ask him to stop yelling at the team."

28
00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:44.004
Pastrami yapped in support.

29
00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:46.006
Or maybe he just wanted food.

30
00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:49.029
Jonathan slipped Pastrami some meatloaf under the table.

31
00:01:52.332 --> 00:01:54.494
He thought about his parents' offers to speak to his coach.

32
00:01:55.275 --> 00:01:56.636
That would make things easy for him.

33
00:01:57.612 --> 00:02:01.333
But how could he complain about his parents babying him if he let them speak on his behalf?

34
00:02:02.393 --> 00:02:03.774
Jonathan looked up and shook his head.

35
00:02:03.794 --> 00:02:05.654
"Thanks for offering to help.

36
00:02:06.795 --> 00:02:07.555
I appreciate it.

37
00:02:08.275 --> 00:02:09.635
But I want to handle things myself."

38
00:02:11.176 --> 00:02:12.516
His mother peered closely at him.

39
00:02:12.536 --> 00:02:14.317
"That's fine, Jonathan.

40
00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:15.577
But how?"

41
00:02:16.057 --> 00:02:16.557
she asked.

42
00:02:17.578 --> 00:02:18.378
Jonathan shrugged.

43
00:02:19.098 --> 00:02:20.759
He wasn't exactly sure what he would do.

44
00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:22.619
But he had to do something.

45
00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:25.620
"Well, we'll back you up," his dad said.

46
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.521
"You can always count on us."

47
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:30.363
"Thanks," Jonathan said.

48
00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:31.844
Mrs. Cho grinned.

49
00:02:31.864 --> 00:02:35.326
"But only if you stop feeding Pastrami under the table!"

50
00:02:36.227 --> 00:02:37.187
Jonathan grinned back.

51
00:02:37.948 --> 00:02:39.729
His parents were pretty smart sometimes!

52
00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.811
By the next day, Jonathan had a plan.

53
00:02:43.571 --> 00:02:45.593
After school he walked to the park across the street.

54
00:02:48.454 --> 00:02:53.025
He found Max there, just as he'd expected, kicking a soccer ball against a wall with his left

55
00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:56.247
foot and then his right and then his left, over and over.

56
00:03:00.149 --> 00:03:02.190
Practicing soccer alone seemed really boring.

57
00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.831
"Can I talk to you?"

58
00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:05.132
Jonathan asked.

59
00:03:05.932 --> 00:03:08.394
Max trapped the ball under one foot and turned toward Jonathan.

60
00:03:08.414 --> 00:03:10.895
"Sure. What's up?"

61
00:03:12.016 --> 00:03:14.037
"I want to apologize," Jonathan said.

62
00:03:14.057 --> 00:03:16.558
"I've been blaming you for things that your dad does.

63
00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:19.900
It's not your fault that he makes everyone give you the ball."

64
00:03:20.864 --> 00:03:21.325
He grinned.

65
00:03:21.345 --> 00:03:24.587
"Just like it's not my fault that my mom calls me Johnnyboy."

66
00:03:25.888 --> 00:03:26.789
Max smiled too.

67
00:03:26.809 --> 00:03:28.210
"Thank you for that.

68
00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:32.133
My dad is very demanding, but at least he doesn't call me a dumb name."

69
00:03:32.153 --> 00:03:34.816
"Whoa!" Jonathan said.

70
00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:38.278
He made his eyes bulge out and dropped his jaw as far as it could go.

71
00:03:38.298 --> 00:03:40.981
"Why are you making that crazy face?"

72
00:03:41.481 --> 00:03:42.081
Max asked.

73
00:03:42.101 --> 00:03:48.026
"Because I'm in shock from witnessing a miracle: Max Wattenbarger actually smiled."

74
00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:49.788
Max smiled wider.

75
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.721
"I should do that more often—it feels good.

76
00:03:53.461 --> 00:03:55.421
I know I take soccer too seriously sometimes."

77
00:03:56.922 --> 00:03:58.062
He hesitated for a second.

78
00:03:58.082 --> 00:04:00.823
"And I need to apologize to you too.

79
00:04:01.703 --> 00:04:04.564
I should have asked my dad to give everyone on the team a chance with the ball.

80
00:04:05.624 --> 00:04:07.385
I didn't want to hurt his feelings or make him mad.

81
00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:12.106
He's so proud of me, and he works really hard to make me a better soccer player.

82
00:04:13.246 --> 00:04:15.947
Plus, honestly, I couldn't get up the nerve to ask him.

83
00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:17.747
He'd get furious at me."

84
00:04:18.888 --> 00:04:20.928
"I should have asked him too," Jonathan said.

85
00:04:20.948 --> 00:04:22.589
"I didn't have the nerve either.

86
00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:23.810
I get it."

87
00:04:24.991 --> 00:04:26.472
"Good, but can you get this?"

88
00:04:29.273 --> 00:04:31.594
Max ran off with the ball, dribbling it through the park.

89
00:04:32.555 --> 00:04:34.736
Jonathan chased after him, but Max was too fast.

90
00:04:35.697 --> 00:04:38.058
Suddenly Carlos ran over and stole the ball from Max.

91
00:04:42.221 --> 00:04:43.681
going," Jonathan said.

92
00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.162
"When did you get here?"

93
00:04:45.182 --> 00:04:48.104
"Just now," Carlos replied.

94
00:04:49.096 --> 00:04:52.798
"I spotted someone dribbling a soccer ball faster than the speed of light, and I knew it had

95
00:04:52.838 --> 00:04:53.418
to be Max."

96
00:04:53.438 --> 00:04:56.520
"Don't exaggerate," Jonathan said.

97
00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.461
"Max doesn't run that fast.

98
00:04:59.562 --> 00:05:02.463
Though he can probably beat most cars, trains, and airplanes."

99
00:05:03.624 --> 00:05:04.304
Max laughed.

100
00:05:06.946 --> 00:05:08.126
Jonathan pretended to faint.

101
00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.868
He said, "Max, you set two huge records today.

102
00:05:12.429 --> 00:05:14.390
You smiled and you laughed."

103
00:05:16.951 --> 00:05:18.452
Soon all three boys were laughing.

104
00:05:19.296 --> 00:05:23.039
Then they kicked the ball around and practiced the double fake and hip fake moves that Max had

105
00:05:23.079 --> 00:05:24.140
taught them the week before.

106
00:05:27.763 --> 00:05:29.464
When they got tired, they sat on the grass.

107
00:05:29.484 --> 00:05:35.329
"A few weeks ago, I only wanted to win soccer games," Carlos said.

108
00:05:35.349 --> 00:05:39.352
"But it's no fun to win soccer if you hardly ever get the ball.

109
00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.554
I'd rather lose and have fun."

110
00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.876
"Me too," Jonathan agreed.

111
00:05:45.957 --> 00:05:46.938
Max nodded glumly.

112
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:51.845
"My dad means well, but having me hog the ball isn't fair to the rest of the team."

113
00:05:52.886 --> 00:05:54.006
Carlos started laughing.

114
00:05:54.026 --> 00:05:58.408
"At one point Jonathan was so mad at you, he was scheming ways to get rid of you.

115
00:05:59.468 --> 00:06:02.950
He wanted to infect you with cold germs so you'd get too sick to play!"

116
00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.491
Jonathan instantly felt bad.

117
00:06:05.511 --> 00:06:07.692
"I wasn't serious about that!"

118
00:06:08.832 --> 00:06:09.452
Max shrugged.

119
00:06:09.472 --> 00:06:10.753
"It's cool.

120
00:06:11.413 --> 00:06:12.194
We're friends now."

121
00:06:12.214 --> 00:06:14.315
"How about a group hug?"

122
00:06:14.755 --> 00:06:15.495
Jonathan joked.

123
00:06:16.335 --> 00:06:17.616
Carlos pretended to throw up.

124
00:06:18.788 --> 00:06:20.229
"How about a fist bump instead?"

125
00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:21.290
Max asked.

126
00:06:21.911 --> 00:06:23.612
Jonathan nodded and held up his fist.

127
00:06:27.015 --> 00:06:31.279
On the way home later, Jonathan thought about how a lot of people had been changing their minds

128
00:06:31.319 --> 00:06:34.702
lately. His parents had changed their minds about contacting the coach.

129
00:06:35.602 --> 00:06:38.345
Carlos had changed his mind about winning soccer at all costs.

130
00:06:39.506 --> 00:06:41.667
And Jonathan had changed his own mind about Max.

131
00:06:42.448 --> 00:06:44.209
Max was actually a pretty nice kid.

132
00:06:44.229 --> 00:06:50.128
"So maybe," Jonathan thought, "it's possible for Marissa to change her mind about me."

133
00:06:51.189 --> 00:06:53.232
He just had to figure out a way to make that happen.
